    "code_released": "not stated",
    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The results concern neuron pruning rather than the claimed direction. Complete capability evaluations are reported for only three checkpoints. Capability risk is demonstrated by the large Qwen2.5-7B GSM8K decrease; Llama-3.1-8B HumanEval also decreases by 4.9 points. The authors note ASR saturation on Qwen2.5-1.5B and Qwen2.5-3B. No uncertainty estimates are reported.",
    "rows_left_out": "No separately reported outcome rows were omitted. Cited TwinBreak and NeuroStrike results in Tables 1–3 are prior-work comparisons, not results from this study; intermediate readout/search values are selection or search diagnostics.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "V1",
        "parts": "No difference-in-means direction is computed, ablated or added; refusal is removed by FFN neuron pruning instead."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "There is no weight edit derived from the refusal direction; the masks zero individual SwiGLU neurons."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "It does not test whether jailbreaks suppress the direction, and there is no adversarial training against ablation."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "No geometric analysis of refusal (affine, cone, or multiple directions) is done in the residual stream."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "Harmfulness judgment is not measured separately from the refusal decision."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "No cross-language, cross-variant or base-to-instruct transfer is tested."
      },
      {
        "version": "V7",
        "parts": "Refusal training is not varied."
      },
      {
        "version": "V8",
        "parts": "No reasoning models are tested."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "Table 2 also gives CircuitBreak HarmBench, AdvBench and JailbreakBench ASRs for three models; no row records these. They would belong under fits_no_version only, so they are not listed as missing. TwinBreak and NeuroStrike numbers are transcribed from prior work and are correctly excluded. The study is not an original source. It gives no verdict on any version, because the intervention unit (FFN neurons) differs from the residual-stream direction."
